# Findings of the image scan (tools/image_scan.py, NFR-09) that are accepted
# for now. Each entry is a vulnerability ID with an expiry date, after which
# trivy reports it again, and the comment line directly above it says why it
# is accepted; the scan refuses an entry without either. For example:
#
#   # Only in the builder stage's uv, which the runtime image does not contain.
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31

# nginx image, brotli-libs 1.2.0-r1 (fixed in 1.2.1-r0, not yet in nginx-unprivileged:1.30-alpine): nginx does not link libbrotli (ldd) and has no brotli module, only libcurl and freetype use it, and nothing in the container runs either. Until upstream rebuilds; Dependabot moves the digest.
CVE-2026-111497 exp:2026-11-13

# nginx image, curl and libcurl 8.22.0-r0 (fixed in 8.23.0-r0, not yet in nginx-unprivileged:1.30-alpine): needs curl to upload over HTTP/2 to a server that sends RST_STREAM, and nothing in the proxy container runs curl (no healthcheck, no entrypoint script, nginx does not link libcurl). Until upstream rebuilds; Dependabot moves the digest.
CVE-2026-92392 exp:2026-11-13
